[2.25, "o", "# Deliver Hosted Service Hardening - Charter\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Complete epic `1vzfT4000` and its remaining delivery work while keeping hosted-service hardening traceable through board-managed stories and voyages. | board: 1vzfT4000 |\r\n| MG-02 | Maintain a doctor-clean planning board and capture major steering decisions in the mission log while the epic stays active. | manual: review mission log and board health at handoff |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- Keep `nix develop -c just keel doctor` clean after structural board changes.\r\n- Use one atomic Conventional Commit per story or planning/governance slice.\r\n- Do not add compatibility shims or legacy workflow aliases unless a story explicitly requires them.\r\n- Preserve mission-to-epic traceability for any new child entities created under this workstream.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while epic `1vzfT4000` still has actionable or unblockable board work that can be progressed from local context.\r\n- HALT when `board: 1vzfT4000` is satisfied and only manual verification or acceptance remains.\r\n- YIELD to human when progress depends on unavailable credentials, external infrastructure, or acceptance steps that cannot be safely reproduced here.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show 1vzfT4000\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mHosted Service Reliability And Secret Hardening\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-09 11:36:38\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-09 11:43:07\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-11 11:51:01\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-11 11:51:01\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m2d 0h 7m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/1vzfT4000/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/1vzfT4000/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Port now ships hosted services and sandboxes through the canonical\r\n  \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport service\u001b[0m surface, but the current runtime contract is still explicitly a\r\n  bootstrap slice:\r\n  ...\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Make service restart and health policy part of the canonical Port service model. (`port service apply -> status)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Harden secret delivery for hosted services and sandboxes. (Port stops treating plaintext runtime JSON as the canonical long-lived secret store for service execution -> First implementation voyage complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Preserve one canonical operator and client surface. (CLI, model, hosted API, and SDK all keep using \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport service\u001b[0m and existing hosted routes -> First implementation voyage complete)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m: Keep the hosted scheduler story explicit and inspectable. (Operators can see policy, health, and restart state in status output and docs without reading runtime files -> First implementation voyage complete)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Port must define restart-policy and health-policy contracts for services and sandboxes in the shared model and canonical \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport service\u001b[0m surfaces.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must implement managed-process supervision that can keep a service running according to its selected restart policy and record runtime health state under the existing runtime owner.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - Port must replace plaintext runtime JSON secret values as the canonical execution input with a stronger secret-backend and materialization contract for \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport service secret\u001b[0m and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport service apply\u001b[0m.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - Port must surface policy, restart, health, and secret-materialization behavior through the canonical CLI, hosted API, and SDK without introducing hosted-only aliases. (uncovered)\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - Port must publish a repo-local operator workflow that proves a service can start, restart, report health, consume a secret, and stop through the shipped Port surface.\r\n    Linked goals (4): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - Restart, health, and secret state must remain deterministic and attributable to one runtime owner so \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mservice status\u001b[0m is stable across local and hosted flows.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-04\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Unsupported policy, secret-backend, or runtime combinations must fail fast with explicit diagnostics and no fallback to legacy JSON-secret behavior.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - The first voyage must leave the board with executable implementation stories and verification paths rather than another service-roadmap placeholder.\r\n    Linked goals (3): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              4/4 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m4/4\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Use hosted and local CLI proofs for \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mservice apply|status|stop\u001b[0m,\r\n    - Use model/runtime tests for policy parsing, runtime-state transitions, and\r\n    - health-reporting, restart behavior, and secret consumption.\r\n    - secret-materialization ownership.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 24 | manual 0\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 4 | manual 0\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 8 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35m1vzfTm000\u001